---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// "Last updated" date in the sidebar. Set this on the day the revised
// notice goes live, e.g. '14 December 2026'.
const LAST_UPDATED = '[Date to be set on go-live]';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Sylfaen Advisory"
  description="How Sylfaen Advisory Limited collects, uses and protects personal data, in line with UK GDPR. A B2B construction assurance consultancy based in Wales."
>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/legal.css" />

  <Nav base="/" />

  <section class="section hero legal-hero" id="top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">
        <span>Legal &middot; Data protection</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="hero-headline">Privacy <em>Policy.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead" style="margin-top: 28px; max-width: 56ch;">
        How we collect, use and safeguard personal data &mdash; written plainly,
        for the professionals and organisations we work with. We hold data
        as a <strong>foundation</strong> to be protected, not a resource to be exploited.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="legal-layout">
        <aside class="legal-aside">
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">Last updated</span>
            <span class="v">{LAST_UPDATED}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">Data controller</span>
            <span class="v">Sylfaen Advisory Limited</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">Company number</span>
            <span class="v">17275026</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">VAT number</span>
            <span class="v">523 1958 92</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">ICO registration</span>
            <span class="v">C1967400</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">Registered</span>
            <span class="v">England and Wales, United Kingdom</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-row">
            <span class="k">Data protection contact</span>
            <span class="v"><a href="mailto:mark@sylfaenadvisory.co.uk">mark@sylfaenadvisory.co.uk</a></span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-foot">
            UK GDPR &middot; Data Protection Act 2018 &middot; B2B consultancy
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="legal-body">
          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">01</span>Who we are</div>
            <h2>The practice responsible for your data.</h2>
            <p>
              Sylfaen Advisory Limited is a construction assurance consultancy
              registered in England and Wales. We provide information management, CDE
              engineering and ISO 19650 services to the UK construction sector,
              and AI governance advice and training to professional firms.
            </p>
            <p>
              We are the data controller for the personal data described in this
              policy. The individual responsible for data protection is
              <strong>Mark Biscoe</strong>, Principal, who can be reached at
              <a href="mailto:mark@sylfaenadvisory.co.uk">mark@sylfaenadvisory.co.uk</a>.
              Our company number is <strong>17275026</strong>, and our ICO
              registration number is <strong>C1967400</strong>.
            </p>
            <p>
              This policy covers people who contact us, work with us or are in
              conversation with us. During an engagement we sometimes handle
              personal data on a client&rsquo;s behalf, such as staff survey
              responses. We do that as the client&rsquo;s processor under our data
              processing agreement with them, and the client&rsquo;s own privacy
              notice applies to that data.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">02</span>What we collect</div>
            <h2>The data we hold, and nothing beyond it.</h2>
            <p>
              We are a business-to-business consultancy. The personal data we
              process relates to professional contacts at the organisations we
              work with or are in conversation with. Specifically:
            </p>
            <ul class="legal-list">
              <li>Names and job titles</li>
              <li>Business email addresses and business phone numbers</li>
              <li>Company and organisation names</li>
              <li>Enquiry and project context you choose to share with us, including through our enquiry form or when booking a call</li>
              <li>Records of correspondence between us</li>
              <li>Recordings, transcripts and notes of meetings, where you&rsquo;ve agreed to the meeting being recorded</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              We do not collect special category (sensitive) data, and we do not
              process consumer or individual-customer data. We only ask for what
              an engagement genuinely requires.
            </p>
            <p>
              Our website analytics are cookie-free and don&rsquo;t identify
              individual visitors.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">03</span>Legal basis</div>
            <h2>Why we are permitted to process it.</h2>
            <p>
              We rely on <strong>legitimate interests</strong> under Article 6(1)(f)
              of the UK GDPR as our lawful basis for processing personal data in a
              professional, business-to-business context.
            </p>
            <div class="legal-callout">
              <div class="callout-label">Our legitimate interests</div>
              <p>
                We process your data to respond to business enquiries, to deliver
                consultancy services, to maintain professional relationship
                records, and to share occasional practice updates relevant to your
                work. We have assessed that this processing is necessary, limited,
                and within the reasonable expectations of professional contacts.
              </p>
              <p>
                You have the right to object to processing carried out on the basis
                of legitimate interests at any time &mdash; see Section 08.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">04</span>How we use your data</div>
            <h2>What the data is actually for.</h2>
            <ul class="legal-list">
              <li>Responding to enquiries and conversations you initiate</li>
              <li>Delivering engagements, proposals and related correspondence</li>
              <li>Keeping notes of meetings and the actions agreed in them</li>
              <li>Maintaining records for professional indemnity purposes</li>
              <li>Occasional, relevant contact about our practice, with a clear opt-out every time</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              We use AI tools, under business terms, to help transcribe meetings,
              summarise notes and organise correspondence. A person reviews
              everything they produce, and no decision about you is made by AI.
            </p>
            <p>
              We do not carry out automated decision-making or profiling, and we
              do not send unsolicited marketing. Any non-essential communication is
              relevant to your professional role and easy to decline.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">05</span>Retention</div>
            <h2>How long we keep it.</h2>
            <p>
              We retain personal data for <strong>three years from our last
              meaningful contact</strong> with you. After that, it is deleted in
              the ordinary course of our records housekeeping.
            </p>
            <p>
              Meeting recordings and transcripts are kept for a shorter time. They
              are deleted within three months of an engagement ending or, where no
              engagement follows, within three months of our last contact. If you
              ask, we delete them sooner.
            </p>
            <p>
              We keep data for longer only where a professional indemnity
              obligation requires it, and in that case we retain the minimum data
              necessary for that purpose alone. Where you ask us to erase your
              data, we action the request within one month.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">06</span>Sharing</div>
            <h2>Who else, if anyone, sees your data.</h2>
            <p>
              We do not sell your data, and we never share it for marketing
              purposes. We use a small number of trusted processors purely to
              operate the practice:
            </p>
            <ul class="legal-list">
              <li><strong>Google Workspace:</strong> email, calendar and document storage</li>
              <li><strong>HubSpot:</strong> our CRM, used to manage enquiries and relationship records</li>
              <li><strong>Formspree:</strong> processes submissions from our enquiry form, and keeps them for 30 days</li>
              <li><strong>Calendly:</strong> booking introductory calls</li>
              <li><strong>Microsoft Teams:</strong> online meetings</li>
              <li><strong>Fireflies.ai:</strong> recording and transcribing meetings, where you&rsquo;ve agreed to recording</li>
              <li><strong>Anthropic (Claude):</strong> AI assistance with meeting summaries, notes and correspondence, under its business terms, which don&rsquo;t allow your data to be used to train its models</li>
              <li><strong>FreeAgent:</strong> invoicing and accounts</li>
              <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> hosting this website</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Each works under a data processing agreement or equivalent terms. We
              may also share data with our professional advisers (such as
              solicitors and accountants) and our insurer, where needed to run the
              business or handle a claim.
            </p>
            <p>
              We will disclose data to law enforcement or regulatory bodies only
              where we are legally required to do so.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">07</span>International transfers</div>
            <h2>Where your data goes.</h2>
            <p>
              Several of the services in section 06 store or process data outside
              the UK, mainly in the United States. These include Formspree,
              HubSpot, Calendly, Fireflies.ai and Anthropic.
            </p>
            <p>
              Where a service is certified under the UK Extension to the EU&ndash;US
              Data Privacy Framework (the UK&ndash;US data bridge), we rely on that.
              Otherwise we rely on the UK&rsquo;s International Data Transfer
              Agreement, or the UK Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses,
              as part of our agreement with that service.
            </p>
            <p>
              You can ask us which safeguard applies to a particular service.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">08</span>Your rights</div>
            <h2>The rights you hold over your data.</h2>
            <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
            <ul class="legal-list">
              <li><strong>Access</strong> &mdash; a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li>
              <li><strong>Rectification</strong> &mdash; correction of inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
              <li><strong>Erasure</strong> &mdash; deletion of your data where appropriate</li>
              <li><strong>Restriction</strong> &mdash; limiting how we use your data</li>
              <li><strong>Portability</strong> &mdash; receiving your data in a portable format</li>
              <li><strong>Objection</strong> &mdash; objecting to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              To exercise any of these, email
              <a href="mailto:mark@sylfaenadvisory.co.uk"> mark@sylfaenadvisory.co.uk</a>.
              We respond within one month and make no charge for reasonable requests.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">09</span>Complaints</div>
            <h2>If you are not satisfied.</h2>
            <p>
              We would always prefer to resolve any concern with you directly &mdash; so
              please contact us first, and we will do our best to put it right.
            </p>
            <p>
              You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner&rsquo;s
              Office (ICO), the UK&rsquo;s data protection regulator:
            </p>
            <ul class="legal-list">
              <li><a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a></li>
              <li>Helpline &mdash; 0303 123 1113</li>
              <li>Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9 5AF</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="legal-section">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">10</span>Changes</div>
            <h2>How we keep this policy current.</h2>
            <p>
              We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date
              in the sidebar always reflects the latest revision.
            </p>
            <p>
              The current version is always available at
              <a href="https://sylfaenadvisory.co.uk/privacy.html"> sylfaenadvisory.co.uk/privacy.html</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer base="/" />
</Layout>
